{% doc %}
  Default exhibition copy for the privacy, terms, and intellectual property pages.

  @param {string} document - privacy, terms, or ipr
{% enddoc %}

{%- case document -%}
  {%- when 'terms' -%}
    <h2>1. Purpose and status</h2>
    <p>
      Maison Tavo is a password-gated cookware and commerce exhibition. The catalogue, prices, materials,
      demonstrations and sample shopping journey are presented for evaluation. This statement creates no
      contract, payment obligation or transfer of rights. Your statutory rights apply in full.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Orders and representations</h2>
    <p>
      Please use only operator-provided test details if invited to try checkout. For the exhibition, treat
      prices, stock and delivery as examples. The three customer stories are fictional. “Cookware that
      outlasts you” expresses the house’s design ambition. A lifespan guarantee would require its own
      published terms and evidence.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Heat, materials and Kansa</h2>
    <p>
      The heat study, layered drawings and Kansa answers explain design concepts. For a real vessel, use
      the maker’s verified instructions for that exact model, especially for food contact, heat sources
      and pressure use. A simulated result carries no safety certification.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Consideration of the soul</h2>
    <p>
      The following clause is optional theatre. The disclosure records no acceptance and has no effect on
      access, cookies or privacy choices.
    </p>
    <details>
      <summary>{{ 'maison.accept_house_joke' | t }}<span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;▾</span></summary>
      <p>
        Upon clicking “Accept the house joke”, the undersigned shall be deemed, solely in the imagined
        jurisdiction of the House, to have sold their immortal soul to Maison Tavo for one imaginary spoonful
        of dal. The House waives all rights of collection. All seasoning rights are reserved to the cook.
        In the event of dispute, the casting vote shall vest in Grandma. This clause is fictional and non-binding.
      </p>
    </details>

    <h2>5. Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Write to the project team through <a href="/pages/contact">Contact</a>. For browser settings and
      personal information, read the <a href="/pages/privacy-policy">exhibition privacy notice</a>.
    </p>

  {%- when 'privacy' -%}
    <h2>1. Browsing and test services</h2>
    <p>
      Shopify hosts the exhibition and supports its cart and account journeys. The cart, account and
      checkout can handle information you provide when you test them. Shopify can also receive technical
      data such as your IP address and browser information. Review how Shopify handles that information in
      its <a href="https://www.shopify.com/legal/privacy/consumers">consumer privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Your browser’s copy</h2>
    <p>
      If you save the optional kitchen questionnaire, your hob and cooking preferences, the email you
      choose to enter and the time of saving are written to this browser. The questionnaire uses those
      preferences to highlight cookware in the catalogue. The email stays in the browser. Signing up for
      house emails is a separate form.
    </p>
    <p>
      The embedded Kansa demo matches questions to a local catalogue and example responses. It can keep
      up to 40 recent messages in this browser. The catalogue request carries no message text. Please keep
      personal or sensitive information out of the chat, especially on shared devices.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you choose to use the microphone, your browser may send audio to its speech recognition
      service to make a transcript. You can type the same question instead.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Information you send</h2>
    <p>
      The Shopify-hosted contact and email signup forms send the information you submit. Use Contact
      for a reply about the exhibition. Use the separate signup form only if you want house emails.
      Checkout testing is for visitors given test details by the operator.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Choices and questions</h2>
    <p>
      Choose <strong>[ Reset Session &amp; Storage ]</strong> in the footer to clear local and session
      storage for this storefront in this browser, including the questionnaire and Kansa history.
      Information already sent through Shopify forms or checkout is stored separately. Use your browser
      settings or any Shopify privacy controls shown for cookie choices.
    </p>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or requests about information you sent to the exhibition, use
      <a href="/pages/contact">Contact</a>. The <a href="/pages/cookie-policy">browser storage page</a>
      explains what this theme remembers during and between visits.
    </p>

  {%- when 'ipr' -%}
    <h2>1. The work and its makers</h2>
    <p>
      The exhibition combines original copy, cookware concepts, images, demonstrations and software with
      third-party materials. Rights in each contribution remain with its respective rights holder. Credits
      should travel with the material they describe.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Traditional techniques</h2>
    <p>
      The Chulha studies draw on cookware forms, materials and skills passed between makers. The Maison
      Tavo name identifies this exhibition. Artisans retain their own names, work and traditions.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Reuse and permissions</h2>
    <p>
      Ask the relevant rights holder before reproducing exhibition photography, drawings or text unless
      your use is already permitted by law or licence. An asset’s own licence governs its reuse. You can
      read and compare the catalogue’s machine-readable facts within the exhibition.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Corrections and rights enquiries</h2>
    <p>
      Use <a href="/pages/contact">Contact</a> to ask about permission or report a rights or attribution
      concern. Please include the page link, the affected material and a way to reply.
    </p>
{%- endcase -%}
